I put the box on the floor and thank her again.
"You are welcome," Nina replies.
I tell her that the portal was a bit slow tonight.
"Yes, it usually is very slow," Nina laughs.
She asks if my confirmation has been saved.
"Always remember to download your confirmation," she advises.
I ask her why that is important.
Nina explains that old messages are often deleted on their website.
The system actually deletes them automatically after a short time.
I nod and open the portal on my phone again.
I find the file, and it is immediately downloaded.
"Then the document is safely saved," I say relieved.
Nina smiles happily and wishes me a good evening.
I wish her the same.
She walks down the hallway, and I close my door.
It is really lovely to have a smart and helpful neighbor.
